cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "candidate-qtl"
abstract: >-
  An evidence-preserving plant QTL candidate-gene triage workflow and CLI
  (primary target: Windows 11 + WSL2; Linux also supported). It combines
  phenotype-first and interval-first candidate discovery with an optional
  source-backed direct trait-gene/locus/variant rescue lane, deterministic
  evidence-preserving ranking and provenance, family/copy ambiguity handling,
  and next-experiment decision support from mapping, reference genome,
  phenotype, comparative evidence, and Wet validation state - assisting rather
  than replacing map-based cloning, without claiming automatic causal-gene
  identification.
type: software
authors:
  - alias: "LightSuzuki"
  - name: "Claude (Anthropic, via Claude Code)"
    website: "https://www.anthropic.com/claude-code"
version: "0.24.0"
license: MIT
